<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mondego</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mondego is the longest river lying entirely within Portugal, about 230 kilometres long, rising in the Serra da Estrela and flowing past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a> to the Atlantic at Figueira da Foz. In the 9th to 11th centuries it marked the shifting frontier between the Christian north and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. Coimbra, on its banks, was an early capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>.</p></div>
